  "query_preview": "/Tuesday through Saturday/... \n\nThe upper-level ridge will be breaking down Tuesday as an \nupper- level shortwave trough moves inland and overhead through \nWednesday. The extent to how fast it moves through the area and \neast is disputed across the long range models, but breezy \nconditions and cloudy skies are the expected impacts. By late \nWednesday the next pattern change is quickly moving in, with \nsuccessive additional troughs expected late week. Precipitation \nchances area wide increase to 10-30% late Wednesday night and \nThursday, and further rising to 20-50% on Friday. These systems \nwill be weak, keeping similar, near- normal temperatures from \nday to day. A ridge of high pressure is likely to build overhead\non Saturday with a return to dry conditions.",
